<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Opium War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839–1842</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Opium War was fought in 1839–1842 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>, after Chinese efforts to suppress the opium trade. British naval superiority forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nanjing">Treaty of Nanjing</a>, which ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>, opened ports to trade and began the era of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unequal-treaties">unequal treaties</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-opium-war.jpg" alt="First Opium War" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Duncan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Destroying_Chinese_war_junks,_by_E._Duncan_(1843).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
